# Inertia Drawer/Sidebar Data Pattern

When a page shows a detail drawer or sidebar for a selected record, all read data flows through **Inertia props driven by URL query params** — not through client-side fetch.

## Core Principles

1. The **URL** is the single source of truth for what data the server includes
2. `router.get` (not `router.reload`) to open/close drawers — updates the browser URL
3. **All props MUST be wrapped in lambdas** (`-> { ... }`) — plain Hash/Array values get corrupted during partial reloads

## ⚠️ CRITICAL: Lambda Wrapper Rule

**ALWAYS wrap props in `-> { ... }` when the page has ANY deferred props.**

Plain Hash values are recursively traversed by `PropsResolver` during partial reloads. Scalar keys inside the hash get filtered out while Array keys leak through — producing a corrupted partial object that overwrites the full one on the frontend.

```ruby
# ❌ BROKEN — plain Hash, partial reload corrupts nested scalars
render inertia: "Page", props: {
  record: RecordResource.new(record).to_h,         # Hash — will lose id, title on partial reload
  details: InertiaRails.defer { expensive_query },  # triggers automatic partial reload
}

# ✅ CORRECT — lambda, treated as atomic unit during partial reload
render inertia: "Page", props: {
  record: -> { RecordResource.new(record).to_h },   # excluded entirely from partial response
  details: InertiaRails.defer { expensive_query },
}
```

### Why This Happens

Inertia Rails `PropsResolver` (v3.19.0) on partial reload (`X-Inertia-Partial-Data: details`):
- **Proc/Lambda**: `keep_prop?` checks top-level path → not in partial_keys → **entire prop excluded** → Inertia JS preserves previous value ✅
- **Plain Hash**: resolver recurses into nested keys → scalar keys (id, title) filtered by `excluded_by_partial_request?` → Array keys (tags, associations) pass through `transform_array` without filtering → **partial corrupt object** included → Inertia JS overwrites full data ❌

### The Rule

| Prop type | How to declare | Why |
|-----------|---------------|-----|
| Eager data (Hash/Array) | `-> { Resource.new(r).to_h }` | Atomic filtering on partial reload |
| Deferred data | `InertiaRails.defer { ... }` | Already a Proc internally |
| Simple scalar (string/nil) | Plain value OK | Not recursively traversed |
| Always-included | `InertiaRails.always { ... }` | Already a Proc internally |

## Controller Pattern

```ruby
def show
  board = @project.board
  columns = board.board_columns.includes(column_workflow_binding: :workflow).order(:position)
  tasks = board.board_tasks.includes(:assignee, :child_tasks, :task_comments, :task_assets,
                                     :workflow_runs, :pending_task_waits).order(:position)
  task = params[:task].present? ? board.board_tasks.find(params[:task]) : nil

  render inertia: "Projects/Board/BoardPage", props: {
    project: -> { project_props },
    board: -> { BoardResource.new(board).to_h },
    columns: -> { columns.map { |c| BoardColumnResource.new(c).to_h } },
    tasks: -> { tasks.map { |t| BoardTaskResource.new(t).to_h } },
    cable_stream: -> { inertia_cable_stream(board) },
    recent_activities: InertiaRails.defer {
      board.board_activities.includes(:actor, :board_task)
           .order(created_at: :desc).limit(20)
           .map { |a| BoardActivityResource.new(a).to_h }
    },
    selected_task: -> { task ? BoardTaskResource.new(task).to_h : nil },
    task_comments: -> { task ? task.task_comments.includes(:author)
        .order(created_at: :desc).map { |c| TaskCommentResource.new(c).to_h } : [] },
  }
end
```

Key rules:
- **No task param** → lambda returns `nil` / `[]`
- **Task param present** → lambda returns full data
- **All Hash/Array props wrapped in `-> { }`** — prevents partial reload corruption
- `InertiaRails.defer` for heavy data not needed on initial paint

## Frontend — `router.get` for Open/Close

`router.get` updates the browser URL. On close, the server responds with `selected_task: nil`. No `dismissed` state needed.

```tsx
const boardUrl = `/company/projects/${project.id}/board`;

const openTask = useCallback((task: Task) => {
  router.get(boardUrl, { task: task.id }, { preserveState: true, preserveScroll: true });
}, [boardUrl]);

const closeTask = useCallback(() => {
  router.get(boardUrl, {}, { preserveState: true, preserveScroll: true });
}, [boardUrl]);

// Drawer controlled directly by prop — no local state
<Drawer opened={!!selectedTask} onClose={closeTask} />
```

### Why `router.get` and not `router.reload`

- `router.reload` does **NOT** change the browser URL — subsequent reloads (cable stream, deferred) lose the `?task=` parameter
- `router.get` with `preserveState: true` changes the URL AND preserves component state

## Cable Stream — Board-Level Props Only

Cable stream reloads should NOT include task detail props — they are loaded via `router.get`.

```tsx
useInertiaCableStream(cableStream, {
  only: ['tasks', 'columns', 'recentActivities'],
  enabled: !!board,
});
```

## Mutations Stay as apiFetch

```tsx
const addComment = async (body: string) => {
  await apiFetch(url, { method: 'POST', ... });
  router.reload({ only: ['taskComments', 'selectedTask'], preserveScroll: true });
};
```

## Date Formatting

Alba serializes Ruby `Time` in formats JS `new Date()` cannot reliably parse. Use helpers from `shared/lib/formatDate` (`formatDateTime`, `parseDate`) instead of raw `new Date(value).toLocaleString()`.

## Anti-Patterns

```ruby
# ❌ Plain Hash prop with deferred props on the same page
selected_task: task ? BoardTaskResource.new(task).to_h : nil

# ✅ Lambda-wrapped — atomic on partial reload
selected_task: -> { task ? BoardTaskResource.new(task).to_h : nil }
```

```tsx
// ❌ router.reload for drawer open/close — URL not updated
router.reload({ data: { task: id }, only: [...] });

// ✅ router.get — URL updated, server always sees params[:task]
router.get(boardUrl, { task: id }, { preserveState: true, preserveScroll: true });

// ❌ dismissed state to work around async close lag
const [dismissed, setDismissed] = useState(false);
<Drawer opened={!dismissed && !!selectedTask} />

// ✅ Direct prop — router.get makes URL authoritative
<Drawer opened={!!selectedTask} />

// ❌ Client-side fetch for read data
useEffect(() => { fetch(url).then(...) }, [id]);
```
